      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A basic protocol for verbal de-escalation in the ED should focus on creating a safe environment first. Always maintain a calm demeanor, keep a safe distance, and use a low, even tone of voice. Start by actively listening to the patient's concerns without interrupting, validating their feelings, and offering clear, simple choices to regain control of the situation. If agitation escalates beyond verbal means, you must know when to call for backup or implement physical restraint protocols.",
